## Shrinker Finding

The decisive blocker is `prefix_break == None`. The shrinker refuses to rewrite
when `!prefix_break.is_some_and(|prefix_break| index >= prefix_break)` at
`core/src/context_manager/tool_output.rs:166-169`; with `None`, every eligible
output is merely counted as `shrinkable_before_break`.

`prefix_break` is computed only when `drop_completed_turn_scoped_items` drops
something: `core/src/context_manager/history.rs:358-361`.

In ordinary finished turns, reasoning is first frozen by
`Session::freeze_reasoning_retention` before prompt construction:
`core/src/session/mod.rs:4072-4098`. The feature is enabled by default:
`features/src/lib.rs:1089-1094`. The retention optimizer initializes its break
at `forced_break`, which defaults to `items.len()` when nothing is already
forced to drop (`core/src/reasoning_retention.rs:90-93`, `131-132`), then only
chooses an earlier break if the cache-break cost is lower (`reasoning_retention.rs:134-145`).
Tiny/ordinary reasoning therefore is stamped `reasoning_retained = Some(true)`
via `stamp` (`reasoning_retention.rs:147-154`). On the next prompt,
`dropped_reason` sees `Some(true)` and drops nothing (`history.rs:732-738`).
Thus `prefix_break` remains `None`, and the shrinker cannot fire even for old,
allowlisted, successful, oversized output. The repository test at
`core/src/context_manager/history_tests.rs:630-657` directly asserts that a
retained reasoning item prevents shrinking.

Mid-turn behavior:

- Active-turn reasoning and active-turn tool outputs are protected by the same
  turn ownership checks, so they are not dropped/shrunk.
- A mid-turn retry can rebuild the prompt, but the active turn ID remains the
  same. It normally cannot create `prefix_break` for active-turn output.
- Dropping/shrinking older finished-turn material occurs only when the next
  turn has a different active ID and the retention decision creates a drop.

